<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Mercury copilot-relay: LaunchAgent template for deploy/nightly/copilot-relay.sh.

  A LaunchAgent, not a Mercury service, because it must run under the OPERATOR's `gh` credential
  and the nightly agent must not be able to reach that credential. `mercury host service install`
  does not install it; that surface owns the operator's `mercury.env` identity only, which is the
  `mercury-nightly` token this relay exists to work around. See
  docs/nightly-self-development.md section 5.2.

  KeepAlive plus the script's watch mode, NOT StartInterval. launchd's scheduled spawns do not
  fire while the `gui` domain is in "on-demand-only mode", which it is for long stretches on this
  host. launchd logs `pending spawn, domain in on-demand-only mode` and leaves the job at
  `pended nondemand spawn = interval` forever. That is how the first version of this relay died on
  2026-10-05. A KeepAlive daemon needs one spawn, and the script owns the cadence from then on.

  launchd expands no variables in a plist, so the @@...@@ placeholders are substituted at install
  time. `kickstart` is part of the install on purpose: in on-demand-only mode the bootstrap alone
  leaves the job pending. Install with:

    sed -e "s|@@SCRIPT@@|$PWD/deploy/nightly/copilot-relay.sh|" \
        -e "s|@@STATE_DIR@@|$HOME/.local/state/mercury|" \
        deploy/nightly/com.mercury.copilot-relay.plist.template \
        > ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.mercury.copilot-relay.plist
    launchctl bootout gui/$(id -u)/com.mercury.copilot-relay 2>/dev/null
    launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.mercury.copilot-relay.plist
    launchctl kickstart -k gui/$(id -u)/com.mercury.copilot-relay

  Verify it is alive. The relay logs a heartbeat on EVERY pass, so silence is unambiguous:

    launchctl print gui/$(id -u)/com.mercury.copilot-relay | grep -E 'state|runs|last exit'
    tail -3 ~/.local/state/mercury/copilot-relay.log

  If `state = not running` and the log's last line is a heartbeat, the daemon was killed rather
  than scheduled: kickstart it again. KeepAlive restarts it after a crash, not after a bootout.

  This header avoids the double-hyphen sequence. XML forbids it inside a comment, and while
  `plutil` is lenient, `xmllint` and Python's `plistlib` both reject the artifact.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.mercury.copilot-relay</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/bash</string>
    <string>@@SCRIPT@@</string>
    <string>--watch</string>
  </array>
  <key>KeepAlive</key>
  <true/>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>@@STATE_DIR@@/copilot-relay-launchd.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>@@STATE_DIR@@/copilot-relay-launchd.log</string>
  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>PATH</key>
    <string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin</string>
  </dict>
</dict>
</plist>
